  <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-20" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;3.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;5.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;A change in leadership for an indirect owner of GNB NGL Pipeline LLC effective March 3, 2025, Robert Bourne retired from his position as Senior Vice President and Chief Commercial Officer. On March 4, 2025, Jonathon VandenBrand was appointed as Senior Vice President, Commercial. As of February 13, 2025, Michael Forsyth left his position as Senior Vice President, North Operations. A change in the composition of the Board of Directors effective May 5, 2025, Robert Phillips was appointed as an independent member of the board of directors of Western Midstream Holdings, LLC, the General Partner of Western Midstream Partners, LP.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="f-21" contextRef="c-1">Q4</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="f-22" contextRef="c-1">Q4</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantNotesRegardingFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-23" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantNotesRegardingFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantCommitmentsOrContingentAssetsOrLiabilitiesTextBlock id="f-24" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantCommitmentsOrContingentAssetsOrLiabilitiesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfAccountingForTheRespondentSPensionsAndPostretirementBenefitsTextBlock id="f-25" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;3. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfAccountingForTheRespondentSPensionsAndPostretirementBenefitsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantChangesInOperationsDuringTheYearTextBlock id="f-26" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;4. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantChangesInOperationsDuringTheYearTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfDetailsOnAccountingForIncomeTaxesTextBlock id="f-27" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;5. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfDetailsOnAccountingForIncomeTaxesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantRateOrOtherRegulatoryMattersTextBlock id="f-28" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;6. Effective July 1, 2025, GNB Pipeline&#8217;s maximum tariff rate for volumes transported from the Western Gas Partners&#8217; Chipeta Plant to Mid-America Pipeline Company&#8217;s interconnect in Uintah County, Utah was raised from $0.02237 per gallon to $0.0228 per gallon. For additional details regarding this tariff rate change, please refer to Docket No. IS25-590-000 on FERC&#8217;s eTariff Viewer.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantRateOrOtherRegulatoryMattersTextBlock>
